# Calculator Gradle App

A simple calculator application built and packaged with **Gradle**, on **RHEL**.

Source code: https://github.com/Ibrahim-Adel15/CalculatorGradleApp.git

## Prerequisites

- **Java 17** (JDK)
- **Gradle**
- **Git**

## Setup

### 1. Install Java 17

```bash
sudo dnf install -y java-17-openjdk java-17-openjdk-devel
java -version
```

### 2. Install Gradle

Gradle is not available in the default RHEL repositories, so it is installed manually from the official distribution:

```bash
sudo dnf install -y wget unzip git
wget https://services.gradle.org/distributions/gradle-8.10.2-bin.zip -P /tmp
sudo unzip -d /opt/gradle /tmp/gradle-8.10.2-bin.zip
```

Add Gradle to the PATH:

```bash
echo 'export PATH=$PATH:/opt/gradle/gradle-8.10.2/bin' | sudo tee /etc/profile.d/gradle.sh
source /etc/profile.d/gradle.sh
gradle -v
```

### 3. Clone the source code

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Ibrahim-Adel15/CalculatorGradleApp.git
cd CalculatorGradleApp
```

## Run Unit Tests

```bash
gradle test
```

## Build the Application

```bash
gradle build
```

After a successful build, the artifact is generated at:

```
build/libs/calculator.jar
```

## Run the Application

```bash
java -jar build/libs/calculator.jar
```

## Verify the App Is Working

If the application starts and prints its output / accepts input without errors, the app is working correctly.



